<title>SPAIN: Spanish regional debt - an overview.</title>
<headline>Spanish regional debt - an overview.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a detailed breakdown of regional debt in Spain:</p>
<p>				     DEBT*			 DEBT/GDP **</p>
<p>		     June 96    1990   BONDS June 96   1995    1990</p>
<p>			   billion pesetas		     percent</p>
<p>  Andalucia	    732     191    236		7.2	 2.8</p>
<p>  Aragon		 105	 7	-		4.7	 0.4</p>
<p>  Asturias		69	17	-		3.8	 1.3</p>
<p>  Baleares		51	 6     15		2.8	 0.5</p>
<p>  Canarias	     121	29     35		4.2	 1.7</p>
<p>  Cantabria	     24	39	-		3.8	 5.9</p>
<p>  Castilla-La Mancha  72	13	5		2.9	 0.7</p>
<p>  Castilla y Leon    142	17     39		3.1	 0.6</p>
<p>  Catalonia	  1,018     212    257		7.3	 2.2</p>
<p>  Extremadura	   77	 4	-		5.6	 0.5</p>
<p>  Galicia		375	48    115		8.6	 1.7</p>
<p>  La Rioja		23	 9	-		3.6	 2.5</p>
<p>  Madrid		 456     116    133		3.8	 1.5</p>
<p>  Murcia		  87	43     29		5.1	 3.4</p>
<p>  Navarra		149	 6    149	     11.8	 0.7</p>
<p>  Pais Vasco	   319	92    245		6.4	 2.9</p>
<p>  Valencia	     441	94    192		6.1	 1.9</p>
<p>    TOTAL	    4,261     945  1,452	     5.7	  1.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Debt columns list absolute levels of debt at the end of June, 1996, at the end of 1990, and the absolute amount issued in bonds. Debt to GDP columns list debt over gross domestic product at the end of 1995 and at the end of 1990.</p>
<p>* Source - Bank of Spain</p>
<p>** Source - Savings Bank Association (CECA) Papers on the Spanish Economy</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8430</p>
